    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The full suite (the sole test class `AcceptanceTest`, which drives the new `coreDerivesAgeBand` checkpoint) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation from an optional `birthDate`, computed against the owner's `registrationDate`, following the codebase's existing conventions for derived owner fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional `date`, editable input) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (read-only `string`) to the `Owner` response schema. I kept `ageBand` as a plain string to match the existing derived classifications (`contactPreference`, `locality`), rather than a codegen enum.\n\n2. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small enum that owns the age thresholds in one place: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), with an `asOf(birthDate, asOf)` factory using completed whole years.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `birthDate` field (with `@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`, getter/setter) and a `@Transient getAgeBand()` derived getter alongside the other derived getters (`getLocality`, `getContactPreference`, etc.), returning `null` until a birth date is on file and delegating classification to `AgeBand`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in the hsqldb (used by tests), h2, postgres, and mysql schemas.\n\nMapStruct maps `birthDate` and `ageBand` automatically by name \u2014 no mapper changes were needed. Logic sits where it belongs: the threshold rules in the `AgeBand` enum, the per-owner derivation as a small transient getter on `Owner`.",
